INT. SHIPPING CONTAINER PICKLEBALL COURT - EVENING

A forty-foot steel container, opened at both ends, its inside painted court-green. Folding chairs line one wall. A net sags between two rusted poles.

ANNIKA STRAND (30s, visor, knee brace) and SOLEDAD VEGA (30s, sweatband, quick feet) face each other across the net. MARCUS BELL (40s, referee, whistle, clipboard) sits on a stepladder at the sideline.

MARCUS
First to eleven. Win by two.

ANNIKA
Marcus, we know.

MARCUS
Just saying it for the record.

SOLEDAD
Serve, Annika.

ANNIKA
Soledad, you serve.

SOLEDAD
It's your turn.

ANNIKA
It was your turn.

MARCUS
Neither of you serves until I say.

They glare. Marcus lifts his whistle. Waits. Blows.

Annika serves. Soledad returns, low. Annika scrambles. She lobs. Soledad smashes. Annika dives. Misses.

MARCUS (CONT'D)
Point, Soledad.

ANNIKA
She stepped in the kitchen!

MARCUS
She did not.

ANNIKA
Marcus, I saw her foot.

MARCUS
Annika, I saw her foot too, and it was behind the line.

Soledad grins. Annika hurls her paddle onto the steel floor. It clangs.

MARCUS (CONT'D)
That's a warning.

ANNIKA
You're a warning.

SOLEDAD
Be nice, Annika.

ANNIKA
She's nice. I'm nice. You're not even here.

Soledad bounces the ball.

SOLEDAD
Eight-two. Want to forfeit?

ANNIKA
Never.

She retrieves the paddle. Plants her feet. Her knuckles whiten.
